    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)`** now builds:\n  - **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n  - **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n  - **NNNN** \u2014 a *per-city* 4-digit sequence, computed as one more than the number of owners already living in that city (case-insensitive), instead of the old global owner count.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n- The **membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) is derived directly from `customerCode`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. I updated its javadoc example accordingly.\n\nTest suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance test asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` format is now green.",
