    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is cleanly scoped and structurally sound:\n\n- The new `city` parameter and the per-city sequence live in `nextCustomerCode`, which is exactly where the customer-code construction already belonged \u2014 logic stays in the right unit rather than leaking into `addOwner`.\n- `membershipNumber` correctly needs no logic change: it's already derived purely from `customerCode`, so the new format propagates automatically. Only its javadoc example was updated, which is the right (and complete) follow-through on the spec's \"rebuild everything derived from it.\"\n- The javadoc on `nextCustomerCode` was fully updated (format, new `@param city`, example), keeping the docs coherent with the code.\n- No new catch-all method or class; the helper set (`nextCustomerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `countNamesakes`, etc.) remains a natural family of private builders.\n- The stream-based per-city count reads naturally and a maintainer of this file would find it idiomatic.\n\nThe only nit worth noting \u2014 the `substring(0, Math.min(3, len)).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)` prefix expression now appears twice within the method \u2014 is trivial: two occurrences of a one-liner inside a single small private method is well within normal Java style and not worth a helper extraction. No structural changes needed.",
